linkedin.mail.account_paused.body:
{trigger, select, limit_reached {LinkedIn restricted your LinkedIn account, or the account reached LinkedIn's weekly limit of connection requests.} checkpoint {LinkedIn asked your LinkedIn account to pass a security check (a checkpoint).} session_invalid {Your LinkedIn account's session ended: LinkedIn signed it out of Whytide.} rate_limit_errors {LinkedIn answered your LinkedIn account with errors again and again within a short time.} acceptance_rate {Too few of your LinkedIn account's connection requests were accepted lately.} other {LinkedIn warned about your LinkedIn account.}}

{trigger, select, limit_reached {Whytide stopped every send and read of the account until {pausedUntil}, the end of its cool-down. After that time, resume the account on its LinkedIn page.} checkpoint {Whytide stopped every send and read of the account until {pausedUntil}, the end of its cool-down. Pass the check on LinkedIn, then connect the account again on its LinkedIn page; after that time, resume it there.} session_invalid {Whytide stopped every send and read of the account until it is connected again. Connect it again on its LinkedIn page.} rate_limit_errors {Whytide stopped every send and read of the account until {pausedUntil}, the start of its next working day. There is nothing to do: they start again on their own then.} acceptance_rate {Whytide stopped the account's connection requests; its messages and reads go on. Whytide checks the rate again every day.} other {Whytide paused the account. Its LinkedIn page says what to do.}}{hasLink, select, true {

{link}} other {}}

linkedin.mail.invites_paused.body:
{trigger, select, limit_reached {LinkedIn restricted a LinkedIn account on this Whytide instance, or the account reached LinkedIn's weekly limit of connection requests.} checkpoint {LinkedIn asked a LinkedIn account on this Whytide instance to pass a security check (a checkpoint).} other {LinkedIn warned about a LinkedIn account on this Whytide instance.}}

The fleet breaker stopped the connection requests of every LinkedIn account on the instance; messages and reads go on. The account itself stays paused until its owner resumes it, and only you reopen the connection requests.

Workspace: {workspaceId}
Account: {accountId}
Trigger: {trigger}
Time: {at}

First read the health of the account and of the instance's other accounts (the linkedin runbook, "The fleet breaker"). Then reopen the connection requests, on the production machine from deploy/:

docker compose exec api node ../../modules/linkedin/dist/cli/control.js breaker reopen --operator your-name

or on a laptop, from the repository root:

pnpm linkedin:control breaker reopen --operator your-name
